.venv/
__pycache__/
# pipeline output: keep the octinoxate results, ignore scratch and test runs
runs/*
!runs/octinoxate/
!runs/oxybenzone/
# The replicate campaign's leg lists (dir:leg lines for racc_feed.sh, one file per batch), and a
# note file beside them if one is ever needed. The staged replicate leg dirs themselves are matched
# by the negations above, like their originals.
!runs/replicates/
# The fold-cofold campaign's leg lists, same rationale as the replicate lists above: these name
# which legs went into which batch job and are the only record of that. The driver that consumed
# them lives in code/feed_chain.sh with the other racc scripts. Logs here stay ignored -- they are
# feeder/drain chatter, not results.
!runs/folds_md/
runs/folds_md/*.log
runs/folds_md/feed_chain.sh
# Run logs belong beside the results they describe, in runs/<ligand>/logs/, which the line above
# already keeps. This negation is only a safety net for one redirected to runs/ by mistake: never
# ignore a run log, because it is the only record of how long a calculation took, whether it
# converged, and what it printed on the way. Regenerating one means re-running the hours of UMA
# relaxation that produced it.
!runs/*.log

# MD artifacts too large for git, kept on disk beside the results they produced. The full
# trajectories are the expensive part -- 2.1 GB of .dcd for four legs of orig_f12 -- and they are
# never deleted, only left out of version control. What IS committed is enough to redo the analysis:
# the wrapped solute trajectory (.xtc), the prmtops, the energy log and FINAL_RESULTS_MMPBSA.dat.
# Rebuilding a system.xml from the committed protein_fixed.pdb and ligand_prepped.sdf takes minutes.
runs/*/md/**/traj*.dcd
runs/*/md/**/traj.nc
runs/*/md/**/checkpoint*.chk
runs/*/md/**/system.xml

# AmberTools scratch. MMPBSA.py writes these into the working directory, so running `omd mmgbsa`
# from the repository root leaves them here. They are scratch, not results, and one of them
# (reference.frc) reached 1.9 GB.
_MMPBSA_*
reference.frc

# Cluster access facts: account-specific, untracked (CLAUDE.md carries the workflow)
RACC.md

# racc_drain.sh bookkeeping: .drained is its per-leg sentinel (a fresh clone must not inherit it),
# tail.log the transcript of that leg's local tail. Neither is a result; the results are the
# mmgbsa/ directories and md_contacts.csv beside them.
runs/*/md/**/.drained
runs/*/md/**/tail.log
runs/*/logs/racc_*.log

# Process logs whose content is fully redundant with committed files (added 2026-10-18 after they
# had been committed in bulk -- ~1,100 of them, none read by any analysis). mmpbsa.log is
# MMPBSA.py's own stdout (setup and timing only; the numbers live in FINAL_RESULTS_MMPBSA.dat);
# the gnina per-structure logs are mirrored in the gnina_local repo, and _scored.sdf is their
# analysis input. The fold- and UMA-side logs (runs/<mol>/{logs,uma_logs,modal,boltz,folds}) and
# the dock/*/vina.log raw scorer output stay tracked: those hold detail no table re-captures
# (per-pose energy terms, box settings) or describe hours of relaxation, not seconds of parsing.
runs/*/md/**/mmpbsa.log
runs/*/gnina/**/*.log
runs/*/md/*_build.log
runs/*/md/*_run.log
runs/*/md/*_produce.log
runs/*/md/*_windows.log
runs/*/md/*_windows_live.log
runs/*/md/*_stability.log
runs/*/md/*_mmgbsa.log
runs/*/md/*_driver.log
runs/tail_*.log
runs/pairs_o3cof_*.log
runs/build_nulls*.log
